==Trivia==
*His English name references the eponymous Shiba Inu that became a [[wikipedia:Doge (meme)|meme]] on the internet.
*His Japanese name, ''Wanko'' (Doggy/Puppy), is the dog equivalent to ''Nyanko'' (Kitty) in that the onomatopoeia for a dog's bark is 'wan' and a cat's meow is 'nyan'. The 'ko' is just a suffix meaning child.
*[[Nyanko New Japan]] and [[Battle Cats Quest]] are the only Battle Cats games not to include any variation of Doge.
*The [[Birthday Cake]] enemy may be a reference to how Doge sends gifts to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] annually.
*According to several descriptions, Doge and his variants are part of a larger Doge clan.
**[[Gabriel]] is the great-grandfather of the Doge clan, [[Zoge]] is Doge's late father, [[Coffin Zoge]] is an ancient hero of the Doge Army, [[Aku Doge]] and [[Wild Doge]] are Doge's brothers, [[Li'l Doge]] is Doge's time-traveling grandchild from the future, an unnamed aunt is mentioned in [[Miss Haka]]'s Japanese description, and [[King Wahwah]] is described as "Head of the Doge Dynasty" in the [[Media:KingWahwahPoster.jpg|event poster]] for [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|King Wahwah's Revenge]].
*Most of the Doges' descriptions involve the education system. Doge is trying to enter college, [[Doge Dark]] works as a part-time killer to earn money towards prep school, Gabriel bites his descendants when they sleep in class, [[Metal Doge]] became a cyborg on his way back from prep school, [[Shibalien]]'s Japanese description says he passed the exam but hasn't adjusted to school life, Zoge worries about his kids' grades, [[Coffin Zoge]]'s Japanese description mentions scholars, [[Shibalien Elite]]'s Japanese description says he is the Galactic University's youngest student to learn Warp attacks, [[Relic Doge]]'s Japanese description mentions studying, Aku Doge pays for Doge's tuition, Li'l Doge came from the future to alter the past where its grandfather failed a test, albeit without success, and [[Dogenstein]] could never finish his final exam in time due to his Sage Gem causing him to overthink every single question.
*In [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], his gender is confirmed in Li'l Doge's description, where it's mentioned that Doge is Li'l Doge's grandfather in the future.
**In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Doge was previously established as male in Aku Doge's description, which refers to Doge as his younger brother.
*In the Korean version, Doge is listed as part of [[Ms. Sign]]'s family structure instead of a "daddy".
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], [[Super Metal Hippoe]]'s description says he came down with a Doge virus.
*He is the enemy with the most variants.
*With the addition of the [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin]] enemy type and [[Kaijin Doge]] in [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]], Doge became the first and only enemy to have a variant for every non-collab type.
**Excluding event enemies and the [[Media:Reddogeship.png|Red UFO Doge]] from [[Nyanko Defence Force]], the only trait without a Doge variant is [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]].
*He is one of the three enemies to have both [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred]] and [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]] variants, the others being [[Gory]] and the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s.
*Despite being the first enemy in the game, Doge has the enemy ID 002, with the two IDs before him being empty.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "with Doge."
*Some of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] are "Doge will always love you.", "A Doge will eat your homework.", and "Doges will run away from you..."

